0,"Full text of ""Braj Bhasha for English speakers""",https://archive.org/stream/BrajBhashaForEnglishSpeakers/Braj+Bhasha+Reader+1991_djvu.txt,Braj Bhasa is a member of the group of languages and dialects descended from the western form of Prakrit called Sauraseni. In terms of the genealogical model on which Indo- Aryan languages are traditionally categorized...,Braj Bhasha,Indo-European
1,"Braj Bhasha - India-Box - All Indian States, Districts & Languages",https://india-box.in/language/braj-bhasha/,"Braj Bhasha, also known simply as Braj, stands as one of the oldest and most culturally rich dialects of Hindi. Speakers mainly use it in the Braj region, which includes parts of Uttar Pradesh, Rajasthan, and Madhya Pradesh.",Braj Bhasha,Indo-European
2,Braj Bhasha,https://grokipedia.com/page/Braj_Bhasha,"Braj Bhasha is classified as a dialect of Western Hindi within the Indo-Aryan branch of the Indo-European language family, specifically belonging to the Central group alongside dialects such as Hindustani, Bangaru, Kanauji, and Bundeli.[1] It descends from Shauraseni Prakrit and...",Braj Bhasha,Indo-European
3,Braj Bhasha | Academic Dictionaries and Encyclopedias,https://en-academic.com/dic.nsf/enwiki/11605837,"Indo-European.Famous Braj Bhasha folk songs or poems include 'Chhaap tilak sab chheeni' by Aamir Khusro, and the popular devotional song ,""Main naahin maakhan khaayo"" by Surdas. Braj Bhasha is also the main language of Hindustani classical music compositions.",Braj Bhasha,Indo-European
4,Braj Bhasha (ब्रज भाषा) — 20 words & pronunciations | Word Map,https://langmap.heuron.com/en/wordmap/bra,Braj Bhasha (also Braj Bhāṣā) is the Indo-Aryan language of the Braj region centred on Mathura and Vrindavan — the cultural homeland of Krishna in Hindu…,Braj Bhasha,Indo-European
5,"Braj Records, Brajwood, Brajbhoomi, Braj Bhasha",https://brajrecords.in/verticals/,Braj Records isn't confined to the past; we also celebrate contemporary music inspired by the essence of Braj Bhasha. Our artists and composers craft modern compositions that pay homage to the region's rich musical heritage.,Braj Bhasha,Indo-European
6,Braj Bhasha,https://www.indianetzone.com/braj_bhasha,"Braj Bhasha - Informative & researched article on ""Braj Bhasha"" from Indianetzone, the largest encyclopedia on India.Braj Bhasha Literature The nature of Braj Bhasha literature is defined as mystical. It is mostly associated with spiritual union of man with the Almighty God.",Braj Bhasha,Indo-European
